    "text": "継続動詞",
    "disambiguation": ""
  },
  "corpusAnswer": "Kindaichi: Continuation Verb, ている:　action ongoing.",
  "explanation": "",
  "explanationLong": "<ol><li><i>keizoku-doushi　(　</i>金田一　<i>Kindaichi</i>&nbsp;)<br>継続動詞<br>Continuation verbs. Verbs that show an action has already started, but not finished when conjugated to&nbsp;<i>~te-iru</i>.<ul><li>Actions performed by someone,&nbsp;<i>yomu</i>&nbsp;読む, \"to read,\"&nbsp;<i>kaku</i>&nbsp;書く, \"to write, \"&nbsp;<i>warau</i>&nbsp;笑う, \"to laugh,\" etc.</li><li>Natural phenomena like&nbsp;<i>furu</i>&nbsp;降る, \"to rain,\" physical movement like&nbsp;<i>yureru</i>&nbsp;揺れる, \"to shake,\" and&nbsp;<i>moeru</i>&nbsp;燃える, \"to burn.\"</li></ul></li></ol>",
